\section{Method}
We fine-tune a lightweight convolutional network on drone imagery collected over twelve wheat fields. Training uses the Adam optimizer with a learning rate of 0.001, a batch size of 64, weight decay of 0.0005, and early stopping on a held-out field.
The detector is evaluated against the published YOLO-based pipeline and a random baseline that assigns labels by class frequency on the same splits.
